  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 19 to 21; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  max-version 21 is below the oldest maintained major (32, as of 2026-09), so the release covers only servers that no longer receive fixes.",
        "  min-version 19 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package.json without a lockfile.",
        "  Every install resolves the ranges afresh, so two builds of the same commit can contain different code, and npm ci - what CI uses - does not run at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "script-without-config",
      "lines": [
        "composer.json scripts cs:check, cs:fix call php-cs-fixer, and no PHP-CS-Fixer configuration is in the checkout.",
        "  ./vendor/bin/php-cs-fixer fix --dry-run --diff",
        "  The command is there to be run, so whoever runs it gets a tool that has nothing to go by - and CI, if it runs the script, reports the failure as the change under test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json), AGPL (composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: appinfo/info.xml min-version 7.3; composer.json states no php requirement.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "No Node version is stated: no engines.node, no .nvmrc, and no node-version in the installed workflows.",
        "  Whoever builds the app uses whatever Node they have, and a build that works on one machine is then not evidence for the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.yml, superseded form), Stylelint (.stylelintrc.yml), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.yml: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "9 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/auth, @nextcloud/event-bus, node-sass, vue-i18n, @babel/core, eslint-config-airbnb-base, eslint-plugin-import, url-loader, and 1 more.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 294 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
      "lines": [
        "Version 0.8.4 in appinfo/info.xml and package.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
